    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Forward and backward differences are O(h), central differences O(h^2); Richardson extrapolation combines central differences at successively halved step sizes to cancel error terms one order at a time, reaching much higher accuracy without ever needing an analytically smaller h (which would eventually be swamped by floating-point cancellation error).">

